{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Targeted navigation</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;a href="{{ basePath }}/rendering"
   hx-get="{{ basePath }}/rendering"
   hx-target="#content"
   hx-push-url="true"&gt;Rendering&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Out-of-band navigation state</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">This docs site renders the header and sidebar as OOB partials, so active links update during content-only navigation.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Response helpers</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">content := partial.NewID("notice", "notice.gohtml")
content.Response().
    Retarget("#notice").
    ReswapWith(connector.NewSwap().Style(connector.SwapOuterHTML)).
    TriggerWith(connector.NewTrigger().AddEvent("saved"))

_ = partial.Write(ctx, w, r, content)</code></pre>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The connector configured at startup decides how those response instructions become headers. With HTMX they are written as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Retarget</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Reswap</code>, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Trigger</code>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">After a form post</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.Redirect</code> sends the client on in the way its library follows: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Location</code> with status 200 for a request htmx made, so htmx swaps the new page into the target without a full load, and a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">303 See Other</code> otherwise.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">connector.Redirect(root.Connector(), w, r, connector.Location{Path: "/orders", Target: "#content"})</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Caches</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code> adds the htmx request headers that decide what is rendered, such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Request</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Boosted</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-History-Restore-Request</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target</code>, to the <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Vary</code> header, so caches keep a page and its fragments apart.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">htmx 4</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewHTMX(nil)</code> speaks htmx 2; choose <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.NewHTMX4(nil)</code> for htmx 4. It reads <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Request-Type</code> and decodes <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Target: main#content</code> into the partial ID <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">content</code>; body requests and history restores render the full page. It omits <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Trigger-After-Swap</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Trigger-After-Settle</code>, which htmx 4 removed, and stream interactions write <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hx-sse:connect</code>.</p>
</article>

